An analysis of the eSPI test configuration and the eSPI emulator driver reveals a missing devicetree `chosen` node. The test enables `CONFIG_ESPI_PERIPHERAL_ACPI_SHM_REGION`, which activates code paths in the eSPI emulator driver (`drivers/espi/espi_emul.c`) that rely on a `zephyr,espi-host` chosen property to identify the eSPI host device.

The test's overlay file (`tests/drivers/espi/boards/native_sim.overlay`) defines the eSPI host node but fails to declare it as the chosen `zephyr,espi-host`. This leads to an `undefined reference` during linking because the eSPI emulator driver attempts to get a device handle for a node that isn't properly identified, and consequently, the linker cannot find the corresponding device object defined in the test's stub driver.

The fix is to add the required `chosen` node property to the test's devicetree overlay, pointing to the emulated eSPI host node.

tests/drivers/espi/boards/native_sim.overlay
<<<<<<<< SEARCH
